Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 09:16:15 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 9/9] Install libraries for mhs with cabal install --lib

mhs has no package environments: it finds packages in the package
directories of its search path, into which 'mhs -Q' installs them. With
mhs, cabal install --lib crashed, as it asked about the package
environments of a compiler other than GHC:

  Distribution.Simple.GHC.Props.getImplProps only worksfor GHC-like
  compilers (GHC, GHCJS), but found MHS

It now installs the libraries, with the libraries they depend on that mhs
does not find already, into a package directory of mhs with 'mhs -Q', and
the C sources and headers of each beside it, where mhs looks for them. The
directory is the package directory of the user,
~/.mcabal-user/mhs-<version>, with which the default package search path
of mhs ends, or the one given with --package-env. cabal then says whether
mhs searches the directory or has to be given it with -a: MicroHs 0.16.9.0
does not search the directory of the user, as it expands $VERSION in its
configuration to its own directory instead of its version.

The package directory of the user becomes UserPackageDB, instead of
~/.mcabal/mhs-<version>, where MicroCabal installs, which is the directory
of mhs itself when it is installed with 'make minstall'. It is left out of
GlobalPackageDB, although 'mhs -L' lists it, so that, as with GHC, what
the user installs does not change how projects build.

The test MHS/InstallLib installs a library with a C source into the
package directory of the user and compiles a program using it with plain
mhs.

